# When a Remedy Becomes Evidence

**Current human choice.** Ruslan selected this essay with the other two in the [current trio](../../docs/current-selection.md).


**E012 · Recommended · Assessment as of October 31, 2026**

An institution destroys photographs it promised to keep and pays compensation. Later, the missing evidence makes it harder for someone to defend against another body's mistaken accusation. Why might the first institution still owe help?

[Read the selected manuscript](../selection-20261018/E012.md) · [Read the original](original.md)

## How the argument reached this point

**September: one of the first ten.** A fresh AI author developed the question, worked from sources, received separate criticism and revised. The imported early chronology below has only later inventory entries; those entries are not invented writing dates. [The initial process](../../docs/generation.md).

**October: reopen a rejected candidate and repair a causal gap.** The fixed rejection check returned E012 for further work. Its earlier argument left unclear why the first institution should help after an honest payment when another body made the later error. The October 17 revision added a case in which the missing photograph could defeat the accusation, and a control case in which the photograph would not help. The obligation now rests on the promised evidential protection and the continuing impairment caused by its loss. A separate review accepted that narrower argument. [Preparation decision](../../evidence/final-selection/updates/20261018/preselection/DECISIONS.json).

**October 19–31: select the revised text.** It entered the main eight and then the recommended three. The later checks retained its specific application while finding close work on substitute duties and replacement-proof costs. Two cited full texts were inaccessible; neither general novelty nor an exact amount of required assistance was established. [The current assessment](../../docs/final-shortlist.md#e012--when-a-remedy-becomes-evidence).

## What to look for while reading

Compare the helpful-photograph case with the control. The argument needs the continuing loss of a promised defence, not merely a later problem following an earlier wrong.

